:: Combat 1 Start
<<run endCombat1()>>
Very basic fishing system, essentially my first draft. The goal is to correctly react to the current of the fish, but this turned into a pick-the-correct-option game, which gets boring fast. At one point the goal was to control the depth of the fish, since having the fish at the surface would make it thrash -> thrashing would make noise -> noise attracts bad attention. But that was janky, and so I dropped it.
<br><br>

<<link [[Herring|Combat 1]]>><<run startCombat1("herring")>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Perch|Combat 1]]>><<run startCombat1("perch")>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Haddock|Combat 1]]>><<run startCombat1("haddock")>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Salmon|Combat 1]]>><<run startCombat1("salmon")>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Cod|Combat 1]]>><<run startCombat1("cod")>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Pike|Combat 1]]>><<run startCombat1("pike")>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Back|Bathroom]]>><</link>>

:: Combat 1
<<run combat1Effects()>>

/* You've landed the fish */
<<if $combat1.fishDistance lte 0>>
	<<combat1Caught>>

/* Your line has snapped */
<<elseif $combat1.lineHealth lte 0>>
	<<combat1LineSnapped>>

/* Still fighting */
<<else>>
	<<combat1Main>>
<</if>>


:: Combat 1 Cut Line
<<set _fishName to $combat1.fishName>>
<<run endCombat1()>>
You release the tension on your rod, letting your line go slack. The _fishName pulls harder, and with a sudden snap, your line breaks free. Through the ripples, you catch a glimpse of it darting deeper, finally free.
<br><br>

<<link [[Fish|Combat 1 Start]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Back|Bathroom]]>><</link>>


:: Widgets Combat 1 [widget]
<<widget "combat1Main">>
	<<run combat1Action()>>
	<<combat1ActionDescription>>
	<<combat1PrintInfo>>
	<br><br>

	<<combat1Actions>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "combat1PrintInfo">>
	<br>
	Stamina: <<print $combat1.fishStamina>> / <<print $combat1.startingStamina>>
	| Distance: <<print $combat1.fishDistance>>
	| Line: <<print $combat1.lineHealth>> / 3
	| Depth: <<print $combat1.fishDepth>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "combat1ActionDescription">>
	<<if $drunk gte 100 and random(1, 2) is 1>>
		<<switch random(1, 5)>>
			<<case 1>>
				<span @class="basicDrunkCss()">Everything tilts. The fish is probably doing fish things.</span>
			<<case 2>>
				<span @class="basicDrunkCss()">You squint at the water. Is the fish doing something or just sitting there?</span>
			<<case 3>>
				<span @class="basicDrunkCss()">Something's pulling your line around. Or maybe you're just dizzy.</span>
			<<case 4>>
				<span @class="basicDrunkCss()">Your hands move. The rod moves. Whether the fish moved first is anyone's guess.</span>
			<<case 5>>
				<span @class="basicDrunkCss()">Your hands are moving. The rod's moving. The world's moving. It's all very confusing.</span>
		<</switch>>
	<<else>>
		<<if $combat1.fishAction is "rest">>
			The fish has stopped struggling.
		<<elseif $combat1.fishAction is "thrash">>
			The fish is thrashing about on the surface.
		<<elseif $combat1.fishAction is "dive">>
			The fish is diving deeper.
		<<elseif $combat1.fishAction is "swim">>
			The fish is pulling against your line.
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "combat1Actions">>
	<<link [[Reel in|Combat 1]]>><<set $combat1.playerAction to "reel">><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Hold the line|Combat 1]]>><<set $combat1.playerAction to "hold">><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Put slack on the line|Combat 1]]>><<set $combat1.playerAction to "slack">><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Cut the line|Combat 1 Cut Line]]>><<set $combat1.playerAction to "cut">><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "combat1Caught">>
	<<set _fishName to $combat1.fishName>>
	<<run endCombat1()>>
	With a final haul the _fishName breaks the surface and you swing it up out of the water.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Fish again|Combat 1 Start]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Back|Bathroom]]>><</link>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "combat1LineSnapped">>
	<<set _fishName to $combat1.fishName>>
	<<run endCombat1()>>
	Your line suddenly goes slack, and the _fishName disappears into the depths.
	<br><br>

	<<link [[Fish|Combat 1 Start]]>><</link>>
	<br>
	<<link [[Back|Bathroom]]>><</link>>
<</widget>>
